The '''Jedi Temple dojo''' was a room where members of the [[Jedi Order]] trained and practiced in [[lightsaber combat]]. Located in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]], [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi younglings]] and [[Padawan]]s alike honed their skills in the dojo. During the [[Clone Wars]], many Jedi, including [[Ahsoka Tano]] and [[Kanan Jarrus|Caleb Dume]], honed their [[lightsaber]] skills in the dojo, practicing various forms.

==Description==
[[File:AhsokaYodaTeachYouIWill.jpg|thumb|left|280px|Yoda and Ahsoka Tano prepare to duel in the dojo.]]
Located in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on<ref name="Kanan 7" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Coruscant]],<ref name="Kanan 7" /> the [[Jedi]] Temple dojo<ref name="Shroud Ep Guide">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/shroud-of-darkness-episode-guide|text="Shroud of Darkness" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars Rebels}}</ref> was a practice hall for members of the [[Jedi Order]]. Any Jedi, including [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]]<ref name="Kanan 7" /> or [[Padawan]]s,<ref name="Teach You">{{FOD|Teach You, I Will}}</ref> could work on simple [[Lightsaber combat|lightsaber forms]],<ref name="Kanan 7" /> be tested against [[training droid]]s,<ref name="Practice Makes Perfect">{{TOTJ|Practice Makes Perfect (episode)}}</ref> or practice [[Lightsaber duel|dueling]] against each other.<ref name="Teach You" />

The dojo was an wide, open space with room for multiple Jedi to move around. Seating was included in the form of [[wood]]en benches for those who wanted to observe training. [[Jedi Master]]s would attend sessions to assess progress, and sometimes, a Master would attend with their Padawan learner to let them witness another Jedi train.<ref name="Practice Makes Perfect" /> The walls of the dojo were also wood and were decorated with simple scrolls featuring [[Jedi crest|Jedi emblems]] or artwork as well as with racks of [[lightsaber]]s.<ref name="Teach You" /> There were multiple entrances to the room.<ref name="Practice Makes Perfect" /><ref name="Teach You" /> For some trainings, a [[force field]] was used to enclose the space and allow a Jedi to train in close quarters.<ref name="Practice Makes Perfect" />

==History==
{{Quote|''Caleb Dume'', maintain your form, you must.''"<br />"''I'll try, ''Master Yoda''.''"<br />"''Do or do not. There is no try.|Yoda instructs Caleb Dume on his forms in the Jedi Temple dojo|<ref name="Kanan 7" />}}
[[File:PracticeMakesPerfect-AltThumb.png|thumb|right|300px|Ahsoka practices in the dojo against new training remotes]]
During the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist Alliance]], the Jedi Padawan [[Ahsoka Tano]] visited the dojo on multiple occasions for training exercises. On one occasion, Tano worked with [[Jedi Master]] [[Tera Sinube]] to train against [[Battle droid remote|new training remotes]] that were designed to simulate Separatist [[battle droid]]s. Masters [[Yoda]], [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], [[Mace Windu]], and [[Plo Koon]] observed the session, with Tano's master, the [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] arrived late. Tano was enclosed in a circular force field in the center of the dojo to simulate close-quarter combat. After being put through the paces by Sinube and performing well, Tano was pleased with her success. However, Skywalker felt that the exercise had not been challenging and left the dojo visibly dissatisfied, which Tano was upset by. The two spoke outside the dojo and then arranged another training session that Skywalker felt was of a suitable degree of difficulty.<ref name="Practice Makes Perfect" />

[[File:JediTempleDojo-Kanan7.png|thumb|left|275px|Yoda working with several Jedi Initiates]]
Some time later, in [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Teach Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[ARC Troopers (episode)|ARC Troopers]]" and "[[Heroes on Both Sides]]" to [[21 BBY]]. As "Teach You, I Will" takes place between these two episodes, the short must take place in 21 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]].</ref> Tano would return to the dojo with Skywalker to practice wielding two [[lightsaber]]s in the style of [[Jar'Kai]]. Yoda soon arrived and asked to see Tano's progress, and although Tano was nervous, having just begun practicing with two blades, Yoda wanted to fight her himself. After Tano struggled, Yoda encouraged her to let her personality fuel her fighting style, which helped Tano's confidence.<ref name="Teach You" /> As her experience with both lightsabers grew, Tano would visit the dojo with her friend and fellow Padwawn [[Barriss Offee]] to spar. Watched by three others, the two dueled, with Tano getting the better of Offee after employing improvisational tactics. Tano was happy with the result, but Offee did not feel that Tano's strategies would work in a real battle and insisted that her peer focus on using the proper forms instead of using tricks. The two disagreed about their fighting styles, but decided that it was a result of having very different Jedi Masters instructing them.<ref name="FOD">''[[Forces of Destiny—Ahsoka & Padmé]]''</ref> Around [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Kanan Flashback">{{HelmetCollectionCite|15|Helmets}} places the events of [[Kanan 10|''Kanan'' 10]] months prior to the [[Fourth Battle of Mygeeto]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places in [[19 BBY]], and ''Kanan'' 7 takes place shortly prior to ''Kanan'' 10.</ref> the younglings [[Kanan Jarrus|Caleb Dume]], [[Sammo Quid]], and [[Tai Uzuma]] practiced their lightsaber forms in the dojo with [[Grand Master]] Yoda.<ref name="Kanan 7" />

[[File:Kanan_vs_the_Sentinel.png|thumb|right|290px|Experiencing a vision, Kanan battles a Jedi Guardian in the dojo]]
Many years after the [[Great Jedi Purge|fall]] of the [[Jedi Order]], the Jedi survivor Kanan Jarrus,<ref name="Shroud of Darkness">{{Rebels|Shroud of Darkness}}</ref> formerly Caleb Dume,<ref name="Kanan 5">[[Kanan 5|''Kanan'' 5]]</ref> experienced a [[Force vision|vision]] of the Jedi Temple dojo while in the [[Lothal Jedi Temple]] on<ref name="Shroud of Darkness" /> the planet<ref name="Lothal">{{Databank|lothal|Lothal}}</ref> [[Lothal]]<ref name="Shroud of Darkness" /> in [[3 BBY]].<ref name="Shroud Date">{{RebelsDate|218}}</ref> He approached a [[Jedi Temple Guard]] and asked for knowledge on how to defeat Darth Vader, but the Guard only warned him that trying to fight would result in his death and cause his apprentice, [[Ezra Bridger]], to become a servant of the [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]]. Jarrus would battle the guard, as well as two others that appeared, grabbing another lightsaber from the wall and fighting with both blades. When Jarrus began to lose the fight and the guard began to taunt him about not being able to protect Bridger, Jarrus realized that the guard was right. Sitting on the floor of the dojo, he and admitted that the could not protect Bridger forever, not even from himself. Jarrus accepted defeat, but instead of striking him down, the guard, who had taken the form of [[The Grand Inquisitor]], [[Knighting Ceremony|knighted]] Jarrus as a Jedi Knight. As the dojo began to collapse, Jarrus' vision ended and he returned to the Lothal Temple.<ref name="Shroud of Darkness" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Dojo-Concept-Art-Shroud-of-Darkness.png|thumb|right|275px|Concept art of the Jedi Temple dojo by Chris Glenn]]
The Jedi Temple dojo first appeared in the comic issue [[Kanan 7|''Kanan'' 7]],<ref name="Kanan 7" /> published on [[October 28]], [[2015]].<ref name="Kanan 7 Date">{{Marvel|url=comics/issue/56101/kanan_2015_7|text=Kanan (2015) #7}}</ref> It later appeared in the ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'' episode "[[Shroud of Darkness]],"<ref name="Shroud of Darkness" /> the eighteenth episode of the animated television show's [[Star Wars Rebels Season Two|second season]], which released on [[March 2]], [[2016]],<ref name="Shroud">{{WebCite|url=http://affiliate.zap2it.com/tv/star-wars-rebels/EP018796240049?aid=dxd|text=Star Wars Rebels: Shroud of Darkness|work=Disney XD Official Schedule|archivedate=20160407082132}}</ref> and was identified in the episode guide published on [[StarWars.com]].<ref name="Shroud Ep Guide" /> For the episode, concept art of the Jedi Temple dojo was done by [[Chris Glenn]].<ref name="Concept Art">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/shroud-of-darkness-concept-art-gallery|text="Shroud of Darkness" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slide 12}}</ref>

